{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Gerrit change 1420 pushed (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1420).\n\nINVENTORY — the survey found NINE derived/parity-gated surfaces, not the four the\noriginal description named. Five had already grown banners since this ticket was filed\n(docs/cli-reference.md, docs/env-vars.md, docs/mcp-reference.md,\ndocs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md, src/rebar/types.py), which is why the description was\ncorrected before the plan review rather than implemented as written.\n\nThe real gap was the two JSON surfaces, which have no comment syntax and so carried\nnothing at all:\n  - src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json\n  - src/rebar/_guides/criterion-pins.json  (found via CONTRIBUTING.md 7a; not in the\n    original description's list)\n\nThree further surfaces are HAND-AUTHORED but parity-gated, so bannering them would have\nbeen actively wrong — they are documented in a second table instead: server.json (only its\nenvironmentVariables block is derived), criteria_routing.json (judgement, no derivation\nsource), and reviewers/*.md (authored body, but front-matter must be a fixed point of\nwrite_front_matter()).\n\nFIXED-POINT VERIFICATION (the critical constraint): both markers are emitted by the\ngenerator itself, so regeneration reproduces them byte-for-byte. Verified against the\ncommitted tree by running each generator twice and confirming git diff --exit-code stays\nclean each time. A marker a regeneration strips would fail the drift gate — worse than no\nmarker — so this was tested explicitly rather than assumed.\n\nGATES: prompt-index, env-registry, CLI-reference, MCP-reference, public-types,\ncriteria-routing (which folds in the guide-pin parity), server.json env-contract,\ndocs-index completeness, and comment-hygiene all re-run locally and pass.\n\nTEETH: three mutations were run against the new test file and each produced a red test in\nthe right place — stripping the index marker, removing the underscore guard in\nload_catalog(), and deleting a docs/README.md table row."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785912962186100001,"uuid":"5c7e283a-3ee5-4e17-968b-c5349e282842"}